# DADGAD Air (repertoire plan: st-dadgad-air). An original 16-bar air in D major, 3/4, in the
# DADGAD tuning: strings 6 to 1 tuned D A D G A D (D2 A2 D3 G3 A3 D4). From standard tuning,
# tune string 6 down a whole step (E to D), string 2 down a whole step (B to A) and string 1
# down a whole step (E to D).
# Every fret number below is a fret in DADGAD, not in standard tuning. The frets used:
#   string 1 (D4): 0 D4, 2 E4, 4 F#4, 5 G4, 7 A4, 9 B4, harmonic at 12 D5
#   string 2 (A3): 0 A3, 4 C#4, 7 E4, 9 F#4, 10 G4
#   string 3 (G3): 0 G3, 4 B3, 6 C#4, 7 D4, 9 E4
#   string 4 (D3): 0 D3, 4 F#3      string 5 (A2): 0 A2
#   string 6 (D2): 0 D2, 5 G2, 7 A2, 9 B2
# Open strings are the drones: low D (strings 6 and 4), G (string 3) and A (string 5) under the
# tune, open A and D ringing beside fretted notes. Let everything ring as long as it can.
# Bars 1-8 in second position (finger 1 on fret 2), with a slide down from fret 9 in bar 7;
# bars 9-15 in seventh position (finger 1 on fret 7); the last bar back to the open D chord.
# Ornaments: a roll in bars 2 and 11 (hammer-on, pull-offs), slides and a harmonic.
title: DADGAD Air
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original air in the Celtic style, in DADGAD tuning
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 7
tags: dadgad, alternate tuning, celtic, air, drones, waltz time
